---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { MIN_DISCOUNT_PCT } from '../lib/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout title="How we verify deals" description="How we calculate discounts and confirm every deal before it's published.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl">How we verify deals</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-6 text-slate-700">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">The {MIN_DISCOUNT_PCT}% bar</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We only publish drops of {MIN_DISCOUNT_PCT}% or more. Smaller markdowns are common and not
          worth your time, so we don't list them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">What we measure the discount against</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We prefer prices we've actually tracked, in this order:</p>
        <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Our own price history.</strong> If we've tracked the same retailer's regular price
            for a product over the past 90 days, we compare against the typical (median) price we
            observed — excluding any days that were already marked down.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Another retailer's current price.</strong> If we don't have enough history at the
            retailer offering the deal, we compare against the lowest price we can verify at another
            tracked retailer for the same product and condition.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The retailer's own claimed price.</strong> If neither of the above is available, we
            fall back to the retailer's own "was" or MSRP price. These deals are labeled separately as
            "retailer's claimed price" and attributed to that retailer, because we haven't independently
            confirmed the number.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Used gear</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          A used, open-box, or refurbished offer is never compared against its own "was" price. We
          compare it against the lowest current new price we can verify for the same product — so a
          used deal always means "cheaper than buying it new right now," never "cheaper than it used to
          be new."
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Two checks before anything goes live</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Every deal is confirmed with a second, independent check of the product page — never just the
          listing page it was first spotted on — before it's published or triggers an alert. If the
          price changed, the identity of the item doesn't match, or the discount no longer clears
          {MIN_DISCOUNT_PCT}%, it never gets published.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
